  "asr_text": "If you're going to learn English words, start with the ones people use a lot. That's obviously right, there's no arguing with it. And yet, the moment a gotcha appears in front of you, the good student inside you steps away. 'That may be true, but what's the rarest one? Wait, you came here to study today, didn't you? The dopa English word gotcha is just the thing to send your mind off track. English word cards have seven rarity levels. The more often a word is used, the lower its level. The less often it is used, the higher. The words you'd want to learn first for study end up on the dull side, in the gotcha. Practical value and star power surprisingly live apart. Normally, you might think, could I use this in conversation? But now you might lean forward and think, What? This word is hardly ever used!? You check the rarity before reading the meaning. You thought you were opening a vocabulary book, but in your mind, a send-off for the rare word hunters is already underway.",
